      "title": "France's Supermarket Fridges Were Vulnerable Online for Months",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "url": "https://ipinfo.io/blog/france-fridges-hack",
      "domain": "ipinfo.io",
      "score": 19,
      "by": "emot",
      "time": "2026-10-20T00:00:49Z",
      "comments": 10,
      "hn_id": 50159616,
      "discussion": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50159616",
      "summary": "On the night of October eleventh, attackers pushed refrigeration systems in more than four hundred French supermarkets into defrost mode, and stores threw out their food. IPinfo's scans found France had about thirteen hundred of these fridge dashboards open to the internet just before the attack, more than the rest of the world combined, and most were running software with known flaws. Nobody knows yet who did it.",
      "summary_source": "https://ipinfo.io/blog/france-fridges-hack"
    },
